// spec = ["§2.5", "§2.3", "§18.1"]

// (S-201, S-89.) E0001: outside a comment and a string, the format characters (zero width space, joiners, direction marks, soft hyphen, word joiner, the byte order mark in the middle of a file) are E0001: they are no space of the language and no name character (§2.5: "コメントと文字列の外では、その他の Unicode の
// 空白（NBSP など）と BOM も E0001"; §2.3: a name is ASCII letters, digits and `_`, anything else is
// E0001). The same characters inside a comment or a string are fine (lex/chars_allowed.onsa). One
// error per function (P-01); each function is named by the code point, the character is written
// raw in the file.

